#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a0aba38-1167-5365-bbd2-cd2ba7e57b15" :question/math-academy-id "e-612" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a39ddf2-3ba2-534f-8dca-93497cae823f" :question/math-academy-id "e-613" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6da4ce70-1718-53bb-8831-a93fdc3e4677" :question/math-academy-id "e-614" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/id #uuid "76a0fefe-71fd-5500-a4d8-7d5f8a09613e" :question/math-academy-id "e-615" :question/problem "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9718da6a-a6d4-578f-a9c3-2f206c80893d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297271} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebd9470-2213-5605-aa8b-ecd8429f99b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297272} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6de13a-1cff-5322-a826-c0d7072def1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297273} {:answer/id #uuid "abddcc28-4e8f-52e1-97ec-9cbdf72a424f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297274} {:answer/id #uuid "82637355-748d-5358-ab04-687b5c68f99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82637355-748d-5358-ab04-687b5c68f99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297275} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f62d617-6d02-5db0-9f4e-3940f13ae4fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52390093-006a-5954-b55c-8b4eeb61a32f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123224" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4c361f-31eb-5c73-b6f0-d6d09b784717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297278} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4a6834-76ae-5517-92d4-424998d1db45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297279} {:answer/id #uuid "d10051ad-4c29-521b-b9c7-3714d1aabdcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{2}}{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297280} {:answer/id #uuid "7e403d58-a8a0-5564-bf33-23e71d03d682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3t}{4}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297281} {:answer/id #uuid "a870ff6f-aca3-5d3a-bfc9-38b70bfe1d98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f4c361f-31eb-5c73-b6f0-d6d09b784717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297278} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fb8b05d-f7e2-5c53-8124-b26c25571fe0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df00f0c0-8884-50e4-8a06-bd7eedd1eafa" :question/math-academy-id "q-123319" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨6{t}^{3}+8,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨6{t}^{3}+8,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{3}+8,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{3}+8)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {e}^{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t+1}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{2}+8t,\\,{e}^{t+1}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "657584f9-862b-5e76-a30d-9c7a11f65045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297285} {:answer/id #uuid "e46ace6a-ff65-5734-930e-f8e769bdd411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297286} {:answer/id #uuid "02a44837-85c1-5223-9eb1-7b33882af019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297287} {:answer/id #uuid "171dbb49-5856-5a4b-a574-0a4958fbd86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297288} {:answer/id #uuid "4d52bd84-87b3-5803-bc6a-fe82b59f6afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e46ace6a-ff65-5734-930e-f8e769bdd411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297286} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9a9868-14fb-53ad-864a-17d45a45d556" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2361e91b-b1d4-5772-97ae-31810eb54d59" :question/math-academy-id "q-123424" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨4{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨4{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 4{csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 3{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa38c1e-5cd2-54aa-83fb-380dd20e2e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\sqrt{15}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297292} {:answer/id #uuid "4092c4d0-cf7c-51b0-9993-253845a00980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297293} {:answer/id #uuid "0c346cb5-c9e6-5084-8db3-f653e51baba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{6},\\,15\\sqrt{10}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297294} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6abd3d-ae0f-56fb-b6bc-8824f28d4f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{6},\\,10\\sqrt{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297295} {:answer/id #uuid "3feae394-1d20-5411-8788-c0fe27686679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{5},\\,15\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4092c4d0-cf7c-51b0-9993-253845a00980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297293} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c04e2b-de81-5c25-81f3-acf002a3439c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ddb6848-feaf-575a-b3b1-c2eb9f0a30e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123520" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{16}⟨\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\sqrt{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{16}⟨\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\sqrt{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\sqrt{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{16},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{(t-1)^{3}}}{3}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{16}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{1},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{(16-1)^{3}}}{3}-\\frac{2\\sqrt{(1-1)^{3}}}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ff2c46-bf01-5472-99ce-9fae200440d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\csc(t)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9ff2c46-bf01-5472-99ce-9fae200440d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\csc(t)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297299} :answer-field/id #uuid "13ee2487-b82e-53be-a770-7e5b07ee0404" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65c95fca-3e13-51dc-a7d6-1b53a4b08f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65c95fca-3e13-51dc-a7d6-1b53a4b08f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297301} :answer-field/id #uuid "b15423ac-0a9a-5d06-8fd9-e7a90583e7e6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dcc9dd5-b778-5f6e-991f-d3af5cb19af7" :question/math-academy-id "q-347095" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨4,\\,-2⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨4,\\,-2⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨4,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨4,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)+3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-1⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1d71b42-f070-5358-9f0e-c4adc08918e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{287}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297304} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e0903d-3a8e-505c-8983-eb7b07a91287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{289}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1d71b42-f070-5358-9f0e-c4adc08918e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{287}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297304} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca78dcba-e03e-55f4-a6b6-697976aae431" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297303} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17cb9437-8362-5fd4-b1f5-853fd91ff2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17cb9437-8362-5fd4-b1f5-853fd91ff2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297307} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8e0d458-8832-5643-adf1-bf6d548ff4bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fadc125-abed-52ab-bd71-19f0048b22b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-349114" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{8}⟨5t-2,\\,\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{2}}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{8}⟨5t-2,\\,\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{2}}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{8}(5t-2)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{1}^{8}\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component, we integrate directly:\n\n$$\n\\int (5t-2)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}-2t.\n$$\n\nFor the second component, we write \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{2}}}=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{-2/3}\n$$\n\nand integrate:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{3}{t}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{1/3}}{1/3}={t}^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{8}⟨5t-2,\\,\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{2}}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}-2t){|}_{1}^{8},\\,({t}^{1/3}){|}_{1}^{8}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 64-16)-(\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 1-2),\\,2-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨144-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{287}{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{287}{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55922e53-210b-5fa5-b670-3946124d8533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{104}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55922e53-210b-5fa5-b670-3946124d8533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{104}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297310} :answer-field/id #uuid "cff1402b-99f4-5108-a3b3-9132dd70b503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297309} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8281c39-3c2d-5572-ad74-9617adfaee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-3e^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8281c39-3c2d-5572-ad74-9617adfaee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-3e^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297312} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec3a91d2-82b0-5be7-936f-57109841dbd7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b006e5b2-6245-5b87-9f41-f85be3078035" :question/math-academy-id "q-349125" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨2{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨2{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{t}^{2}-t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}3{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int (2{t}^{2}-t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int 3{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=3\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})=-3{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨2{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4},\\,(-3{e}^{-t}){|}_{0}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{2}{3}(64)-\\frac{1}{2}(16))-0,\\,(-3{e}^{-4})-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{128}{3}-8),\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0c6ff27-9471-5a2f-ab38-fae61b711c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c6ff27-9471-5a2f-ab38-fae61b711c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297315} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb7dace-5b5c-5f36-83ed-5fef89ac886c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "889e2b17-059e-5003-bed7-ea3e1142dd14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "889e2b17-059e-5003-bed7-ea3e1142dd14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297317} :answer-field/id #uuid "618d9a77-1494-517b-88d6-a861903a0587" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38fa20a5-69c7-5d73-82b7-ef72ada1eb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-349150" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{-1}^{3}({t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2{t}^{3}-t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int ({t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int (2{t}^{3}-t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{-1}^{3},\\,(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{-1}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{1}{3}(27)+\\frac{1}{2}(9))-(\\frac{1}{3}(-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1)),\\,(\\frac{1}{2}(81)-\\frac{1}{2}(9))-(\\frac{1}{2}(1)-\\frac{1}{2}(1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(9+\\frac{9}{2})-(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(36)-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{40}{3},\\,36⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{40}{3},\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8500ecfa-7f69-5692-8378-8a2da6c8d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8500ecfa-7f69-5692-8378-8a2da6c8d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297320} :answer-field/id #uuid "d017f787-38e7-5ada-9e05-3e69d1b615f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4279aaa-49fe-5b0c-891a-825cbf2ec989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4279aaa-49fe-5b0c-891a-825cbf2ec989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297322} :answer-field/id #uuid "492cfa94-52ea-559a-bd8d-87c09d8c7730" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b119c5-e8c6-574b-9b80-220999d2b97b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349193" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩ \\\\ ⟨8+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-6$ and ${c}_{2}=0.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47116129-dd17-52d4-a5cd-17af6222ec30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297325} {:answer/id #uuid "f08e59e7-415b-5c8f-848d-703d8961f906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f08e59e7-415b-5c8f-848d-703d8961f906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297326} :answer-field/id #uuid "72198386-eade-5d65-9626-89b803a74bc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538658d4-48db-5016-9c74-59d88403fe3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\sqrt{t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "538658d4-48db-5016-9c74-59d88403fe3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\sqrt{t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297328} :answer-field/id #uuid "6796ce46-7bea-5098-b314-78af4b163782" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0bced7b-54b7-5ffb-932d-ddddf77d652e" :question/math-academy-id "q-349355" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,2{t}^{\\frac{3}{2}}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+{c}_{1},\\,2(0)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+2,\\,2{t}^{3/2}-1⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "348dfb6b-156c-5f49-8ff1-a8ffea3ef788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297331} {:answer/id #uuid "051549aa-9304-567f-ae68-d83f622120a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297332} {:answer/id #uuid "02acfd0b-8b6f-5645-b4ec-17b11e1ade16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297333} {:answer/id #uuid "672da137-8e68-5ffb-8f60-f86e38a3d560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297334} {:answer/id #uuid "98252e08-446c-524b-b96d-bfc403302007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "051549aa-9304-567f-ae68-d83f622120a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297332} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cf0cf58-3f65-5a6e-b923-9bb799a5f6c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4e000d9-7155-5530-bc95-f9ed61c5c6a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-50078" :question/problem "$\\int ⟨{e}^{-t},\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{-t},\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80530319-a6b8-55b9-b731-4ad7a4a59618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- ⟨e^{t} - 4t, \\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095708} {:answer/id #uuid "e72a7913-4e20-5a4f-a654-a1c67970257e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t},-\\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095709} {:answer/id #uuid "46a55a84-cf37-5290-a61f-d84df6936650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - 4t,-\\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095710} {:answer/id #uuid "54d4ed94-c606-5048-9de8-699236ff79a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - 4t, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095711} {:answer/id #uuid "599e1a14-9e35-5198-93b5-4a66b496dbe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - 4t, \\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46a55a84-cf37-5290-a61f-d84df6936650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - 4t,-\\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095710} :answer-field/id #uuid "48f6bbb6-84b4-5734-8cf4-b84cb1b06c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38244b69-b2ff-532d-ba91-ffcf585c5c43" :question/math-academy-id "q-50202" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$, then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int ({e}^{t}-4)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a2d67e-13a8-5a84-ab13-c3c5e843e9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2e^{2t},-\\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095714} {:answer/id #uuid "0399a4e6-9b75-529f-9e5b-e28dea127114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095715} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb63997-87d9-51b3-9ec9-9aac82e68587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095716} {:answer/id #uuid "63002e0e-db0b-5ef3-88a3-0a9902f7bfe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095717} {:answer/id #uuid "63c5bef5-1cd5-593e-adbd-cd507df93001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2e^{t},-\\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0399a4e6-9b75-529f-9e5b-e28dea127114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095715} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a1bf073-4db0-5a09-aecc-ff3e23e8c2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bad6949-79b1-5ca9-94b6-1b4bffc3a4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-50204" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0580506-5e62-5af0-b3e6-9353b6e3a483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t^{3},-e^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096068} {:answer/id #uuid "ff40ef8b-f310-58f1-8550-e3bacbd522af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t^{3}, e^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096069} {:answer/id #uuid "078c6504-67e7-59f9-a84a-4f8effd83cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t^{3},-te^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096070} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd4ff92-eae2-5a08-baec-0b970b9dc151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{t^{3}}{3}, e^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096071} {:answer/id #uuid "521fd3ba-e41e-5d76-b588-35b2fd32cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3t^{3}, te^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff40ef8b-f310-58f1-8550-e3bacbd522af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t^{3}, e^{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096069} :answer-field/id #uuid "382ef6af-e68a-5f50-9931-43fdb4f90540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22f82dbd-7046-58bc-9a39-900370a35623" :question/math-academy-id "q-80460" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0253e6b-be11-5dc1-99d5-7426ec4d4c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297338} {:answer/id #uuid "7c94ed39-4373-551c-b06c-a1face0ceeb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297339} {:answer/id #uuid "26a71e89-29b4-5bc7-9b10-b54090db6210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297340} {:answer/id #uuid "c6110327-632b-5e5f-bf7a-0617a23a71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297341} {:answer/id #uuid "654378c7-1b93-5365-9376-0fbd0c1eddff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26a71e89-29b4-5bc7-9b10-b54090db6210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297340} :answer-field/id #uuid "b59ed963-fef5-5a46-8d25-f85418d99e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "978f19ce-bf8b-567e-979e-75fe1636e0f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99264" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\text{ }5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 5{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{1}{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d37d18-3912-50ae-b119-91d0fc0c17cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297345} {:answer/id #uuid "22569959-9b54-5299-81f3-e9d010cf0d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297346} {:answer/id #uuid "62a0c73d-9e96-554a-9887-b3e32f13b39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297347} {:answer/id #uuid "7217fed4-5f1d-5f3d-9e8f-6d5be5c8665a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,{csc}^{2}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297348} {:answer/id #uuid "924788dc-2952-5e43-9bcf-bebbdcd19361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22569959-9b54-5299-81f3-e9d010cf0d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297346} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb6dbc62-ffad-5716-b2e6-338bccb0282b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c999e655-1f88-54f4-a90f-5c566eaba127" :question/math-academy-id "q-99268" :question/problem "$\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int -\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12813cd4-e446-54c7-97d8-b20f24924629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297352} {:answer/id #uuid "81d2fa57-7251-5e5c-bb91-670a36a38485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,\\,2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297353} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fc81b2-1aa7-57e3-acb5-d8e9b0bf6ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297354} {:answer/id #uuid "aa213fb5-f039-5bf4-93e1-feaf75499e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297355} {:answer/id #uuid "6c50d982-47ba-526a-a751-64e67930e65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa213fb5-f039-5bf4-93e1-feaf75499e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297355} :answer-field/id #uuid "a165d197-792d-51ca-a35c-beefe49cf864" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f24cce4-3316-593f-909a-7953ae6cdae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99350" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\text{d}t={e}^{t}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ae2db3b-49e6-5911-8adb-36468474b8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297359} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e38e97-5f12-59b6-b616-ea30f2a42749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297360} {:answer/id #uuid "c18ed17f-2440-5540-93e3-19da6caaafb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297361} {:answer/id #uuid "016bcfe3-94ae-5601-a3b8-1c85ae544a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\sqrt{2},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297362} {:answer/id #uuid "c49f4764-bf9d-5b6f-90ae-2114b5bbd7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c18ed17f-2440-5540-93e3-19da6caaafb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297361} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4686a7-fd0f-5125-ac8e-3034077d153b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce4de9d0-a35b-5282-8a54-5ba3b82cc5ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-99366" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi /4)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi /4)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0,\\,1-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a99672-6130-5757-97a9-b83c8b12152d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297366} {:answer/id #uuid "c1352cdf-a45a-5473-8cb5-e42a88c50278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297367} {:answer/id #uuid "754a9675-1fba-57e7-b5df-c41e907a83ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{4}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297368} {:answer/id #uuid "647b7987-adbd-5e6d-92f8-a6c276eebf61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297369} {:answer/id #uuid "c94e23ed-1753-5650-a1c1-b6caad8e1766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}+2,\\,{t}^{4}{-}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1352cdf-a45a-5473-8cb5-e42a88c50278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c88d0d3d-3348-569a-ae2e-19e781544506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac793faa-32dd-5854-af7f-a8fbffd850cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-99517" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3(t-1)^{2},4\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3(t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (4{t}^{3}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{4}-t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨{((1)-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{4}-(1)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "490597ec-c45d-5242-a457-4499ead33105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,{2}^{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297373} {:answer/id #uuid "a5982c98-dd59-5886-aa98-5bc604eb172f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297374} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5d585f-817f-54a3-b2ab-036662f81ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297375} {:answer/id #uuid "796e8910-a230-5f5f-9ad7-35ae4bc416a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297376} {:answer/id #uuid "c55bec89-84a7-5ab8-9496-3aba2affd051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5982c98-dd59-5886-aa98-5bc604eb172f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297374} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b0c5dac-ad1d-52e4-98e4-b4f34092336a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "679c8eba-9d63-5e58-9520-a2c190d788d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-99586" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,0⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (\\sqrt{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {2}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,0⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{2(1)^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{{2}^{1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\frac{7}{6}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=\\frac{5}{6}$ and ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$ Consequently\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
